<title>FINLAND: Nokia wins $40 million handset order.</title>
<headline>Nokia wins $40 million handset order.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecommunications group Nokia Oy said in a statement on Tuesday it had won a $40 million order for GSM 1900 phones and wireless accessories from Aerial Communications in the U.S..</p>
<p>&quot;The contract calls for delivery of Nokia 2190e phones (GSM 1900) and wireless accessories,&quot; Nokia said.</p>
<p>In 1996, Aerial selected Nokia the sole infrastructure supplier for initial construction of its PCS network, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
